  @.7196 link "Section 14.1" url=$u1
  @.7198 text ") that the recipient does not understand, the recipient MUST NOT attempt to recombine it with a stored representation. A proxy that receives such a message SHOULD forward it downstream.Content-Range might also be sent as a request modifier to request a partial PUT, as described in "
  @.7204 link "Section 14.5" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#partial.PUT"
  @.7206 text ", based on private agreements between client and origin server. A server MUST ignore a Content-Range header field received in a request with a method for which Content-Range support is not defined.For byte ranges, a sender SHOULD"
  @.7211 text " indicate the complete length of the representation from which the range has been extracted, unless the complete length is unknown or difficult to determine. An asterisk character ("*") in place of the complete-length indicates that the representation length was unknown when the header field was generated."
  @.7212 text "The following example illustrates when the complete length of the selected representation is known by the sender to be 1234 bytes:"
  @.7213 text "Content-Range: bytes 42-1233/1234
"
  @.7214 text "and this second example illustrates when the complete length is unknown:"
  @.7215 text "Content-Range: bytes 42-1233/*
"
  @.7216 text "A Content-Range field value is invalid if it contains a "
  @.7217 link "range-resp" u
