  @.8037 text "The 302 (Found) status code indicates that the target resource resides temporarily under a different URI. Since the redirection might be altered on occasion, the client ought to continue to use the target URI for future requests.The server SHOULD generate a "
  @.8041 link "Location" url=$u2
  @.8043 text " header field in the response containing a URI reference for the different URI. The user agent MAY use the Location field value for automatic redirection. The server's response content usually contains a short hypertext note with a hyperlink to the different URI(s).Note: For historical reasons, a user agent MAY change the request method from POST to GET for the subsequent request. If this behavior is undesired, the "
  @.8050 link "307 (Temporary Redirect)" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#status.307"
